    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\(x = 3\\) into the expression \\(2x + 5\\).\n2. Calculate the result of the expression inside the parentheses.\n3. Square the result obtained in step 2.\n\nLet's go through each step in detail.\n\nStep 1: Substitute \\(x = 3\\) into the expression \\(2x + 5\\).\n\\[2x + 5 = 2(3) + 5\\]\n\\[2(3) + 5 = 6 + 5\\]\n\\[6 + 5 = 11\\]\n\nStep 2: Calculate the result of the expression inside the parentheses.\nThe expression inside the parentheses is now \\(11\\).\n\nStep 3: Square the result obtained in step 2.\n\\[11^2 = 11 \\times 11\\]\n\\[11 \\times 11 = 121\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\) is \\(\\boxed{121}\\).",
